# Track D (D1b, review round 1 / B1): keeps the Docker build context this
# repo is used as (via `docker build --build-context graphite-context=<this
# checkout>` in the studio repo's Dockerfile/web/Dockerfile) small and fast.
# Without this, `target/` alone (multi-GB Rust build artifacts) would be
# sent to the Docker daemon on every build. `.git/` is DELIBERATELY kept
# (not excluded): the studio Dockerfiles' graphite-builder stage reads
# `git -C /graphite rev-parse HEAD` to verify the exact commit it was
# actually given matches the pinned ref it was told to expect, rather than
# trusting the build-context path's contents blindly.
target/
frontend/dist/
frontend/node_modules/
